<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell 50,000/T of October  naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell 50,000/T of October  naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has tendered to sell 50,000 tonnes of naphtha for lifting in early October, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The first tender is offering 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha lifting October 3-5 and the second, 25,000 tonnes of low aromatic naphtha lifting October 7-9.</p>
<p>Both cargoes are to be loaded from Madras on the east coast.</p>
<p>The tenders close on September 19 with validity through to September 20.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
